# DELIBERATELY NOT OWNED, and the hole it leaves: `justfile` (its `gate` recipe),
# `.pre-commit-config.yaml`, `mise.toml`, `.agents/` (skill text agents follow),
# the Dockerfiles, `.env.example`, the other scripts, `backend/pyproject.toml`
# (the import-linter contracts, pytest options, ruff rules), `frontend/package.json`
# (the scripts the gate runs), the lint and test configs, `backend/app/core/config.py`
# (session cookie settings) and `backend/tests/`. An agent PR that edits one can
# weaken the check that judges agent PRs and merge without the operator. They are
# unowned because owning them sends every dependency bump and every new setting
# or test to the operator too; that trade is the operator's to make, not a default.
#
# Also not owned, by the operator's decision on 2026-11-10: migrations
# (`backend/app/persistence/alembic/`) and the guarded router list
# (`backend/app/api/routers.py`). Schema and new endpoints are routine
# development, and owning them sent almost every feature PR to the operator.
# What still stands between an agent and a bad migration: CI runs
# `alembic upgrade head` and `alembic check` against real Postgres, the
# migration heuristic (`scripts/check-migration-required.sh`, owned) fails a
# model change without one, and docs/review/rollback.md says how to step back.
# A router added to the guarded list is behind the session guard by
# construction, and `test_router_protection.py` demands a 401 from every
# endpoint off its open list; making one public still needs `app/main.py`.
